# Implementation Plan - Sprint "Holistic Expansion"

# Goal Description
We are expanding the Gurudevi platform to include a fully functional **Library**, **Community** spaces, refined **User Roles**, **Pricing Tiers**, and a **Rewards System**. This plan ensures a holistic integration with the existing architecture, prioritizing scale, security, and user experience.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Schema Changes**: This plan introduces several new tables and modifications to existing ones. We need to ensure these migrations are handled carefully if there is existing production data (unlikely for v0.1, but good practice).

> [!WARNING]
> **RLS Policies**: With the introduction of "Public" vs "Private" library items and "Anonymous" community posts, RLS policies will become more complex. We must verify that anonymous posts cannot be traced back to the user by other users via the API.

> [!NOTE]
> **Search Strategy**: We will use PostgreSQL's built-in full-text search for v0.1. For v1.0, we might need a dedicated search service if scale increases significantly.

## Proposed Changes

### Database Extensions (Supabase)

#### [NEW] Library Schema
- `library_items`: Core table for all resources.
    - `id`, `school_id` (nullable for public), `uploader_id`, `title`, `description`, `type` (pdf, video, link, etc.), `url`, `metadata` (jsonb for extradata like video duration), `created_at`.
    - `is_public` (boolean), `is_curated` (boolean).
- `library_collections`: For "Teacher's Personal Desk".
    - `id`, `user_id`, `name` (e.g., "My Desk", "Math Favorites"), `created_at`.
- `library_collection_items`: Join table.
    - `collection_id`, `item_id`, `added_at`.
- `library_interactions`:
    - `item_id`, `user_id`, `type` (like, view, download), `created_at`.

#### [NEW] Community Schema
- `community_posts`:
    - `id`, `school_id`, `author_id` (nullable for anonymous?), `type` (announcement, post, poll), `title`, `content`, `metadata` (jsonb for poll options, images), `is_anonymous` (boolean), `created_at`.
- `community_reactions`:
    - `post_id`, `user_id`, `reaction` (emoji code), `created_at`.
- `community_votes`: For polls.
    - `post_id`, `user_id`, `option_index`, `created_at`.

#### [NEW] Gamification & Growth (Rewards & Pricing)
- `user_rewards`:
    - `user_id`, `points_balance`, `lifetime_points`, `level`.
- `reward_logs`: History of points earned.
    - `user_id`, `action_type`, `points`, `created_at`.
- `gift_codes`:
    - `code` (unique), `type` (pro_subscription, points), `value`, `is_redeemed`, `redeemed_by`, `redeemed_at`.
- `pricing_subscriptions`: (Refining existing structure)
    - `user_id`, `tier` (free, pro, premium), `status`, `valid_until`.

### Mobile App (Expo/React Native)

#### [MODIFY] User Context & Auth
- Update `useUserStore` to include `pricing_tier`, `points`, and refined `role` capabilities.
- Implement "Gift Code Redemption" screen in Profile or Settings.

#### [NEW] Library Tab (`apps/gurudevi-mobile/app/(app)/library/`)
- `index.tsx`: Main view with tabs "Public Library" | "My Desk".
- `components/ResourceCard.tsx`: Display resource info, thumbnails, "Add to Desk" button.
- `components/LibrarySearch.tsx`: Search bar with category filters.
- `desk.tsx`: View for teacher's personal collections.

#### [NEW] Community Tab (`apps/gurudevi-mobile/app/(app)/community/`)
- `index.tsx`: Feed view.
- `components/PostCard.tsx`: Handles different types (Text, Image, Poll).
- `components/CreatePostFAB.tsx`: Floating action button to create different post types.
- `components/PollView.tsx`: Interactive poll component.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- We will rely on manual verification for UI components in this phase as we are building initial prototypes.
- For Database, we can write a simple script to verify RLS policies if needed, but manual testing via the app (logging in as different users) is preferred for v0.1 speed.

### Manual Verification
1.  **Role Testing**:
    - Log in as **Teacher**: Verify "Personal Desk" access and "Create Post" capabilities.
    - Log in as **Principal**: Verify "Announcement" creation.
    - Log in as **Student**: Verify they CANNOT see "Teacher Desk" but CAN see "Public Library".
2.  **Library Flow**:
    - Upload a resource (Teacher).
    - Search for it (Student).
    - Add to "My Desk" (Teacher).
3.  **Community Flow**:
    - Post an announcement (Principal).
    - React to it (Student).
    - Create a poll (Teacher).
    - Vote on it (Student) and verify real-time updates (if implemented) or refresh updates.
4.  **Pricing/Rewards**:
    - Redeem a gift code and verify User Tier updates.
    - Perform an action (e.g., upload resource) and verify Point balance increases (if logic hooked up).
